  "generated_text": "1. We need to count the number of seven-letter good words.\n2. A good word must follow the rules:\n   - $A$ cannot be immediately followed by $B$.\n   - $B$ cannot be immediately followed by $C$.\n   - $C$ cannot be immediately followed by $A$.\n\n3. Let's consider the structure of a good word:\n   - The first letter can be $A$, $B$, or $C$.\n   - For each subsequent position, there are 2 choices (either $A$ or $C$ since it can't follow the previous letter).\n\n4. Therefore, for a seven-letter good word:\n   - The first position has 3 choices.\n   - Each of the remaining 6 positions has 2 choices.\n\n5. Thus, the total number of seven-letter good words is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 2^6\n   \\]\n\n6. Calculating this gives:\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 64 = 192\n   \\]\n\nSo, the number of seven-letter good words is:\n\n\\boxed{192}",
  "grade": {
    "error": null,
    "extracted_answer": "[192, '192']",
    "gold_answer": "There are three choices for the first letter and two choices for each subsequent letter, so there are $3\\cdot2^{n-1}\\ n$-letter good words.  Substitute $n=7$ to find there are $3\\cdot2^6=\\boxed{192}$ seven-letter good words.",
    "is_correct": true
  },
